 "result": "I created two files in the repository root. I couldn't build or run the image here, so neither file has been tested.\n\n- **`Dockerfile`** is a two-stage build.\n  - **Frontend:** a Node 22 stage runs `npm ci` and `npm run build` for the Vite/React frontend. It leaves `VITE_API_BASE_URL` empty by default so the browser calls the API on the same origin.\n  - **Runtime:** a `python:3.11-slim` stage installs `requirements.txt`, minus its testing and dev section, then `pip install --no-deps -e .`. It copies in `src/`, the configs, `models/` and `scripts/`, and adds the built frontend at `/app/frontend/dist`, where the API looks for it.\n  - **Run settings:** it runs as a non-root user and starts `uvicorn climatevision.api.main:app` on port 8000, the same command as `run_api.sh`. There is a healthcheck on `/api/health`. `/app/outputs` is a volume that holds the SQLite database, uploads and audit logs.\n- **`.dockerignore`** keeps `.git`, virtualenvs, `node_modules`, `.env`, `secrets/`, `outputs/`, notebooks, docs and caches out of the build context.\n\nPass secrets at runtime, for example `docker run --env-file .env -v $PWD/secrets:/app/secrets:ro -p 8000:8000 <image>`.\n\n- **numpy pin:** `setup.py` pins `numpy<2`, which could clash with the newer `torch` in `requirements.txt`. That is why the editable install uses `--no-deps`.\n- **`osmnx`:** it is optional and not in `requirements.txt`, so the flood road-impact feature will report itself as unavailable unless you add it.",
